# i18n & theme

## Precedence

1. Explicit user choice in `localStorage` (`svg3dx-studio-locale` / `svg3dx-studio-color-scheme`)
2. Else browser: language via `navigator.languages`, color via `prefers-color-scheme`
3. Persist **only** inside `setLocale` / `setColorScheme` — never write defaults on first load

Use `@/i18n` and `@/theme`. Keep `theme-mode` + `data-theme` on `<html>` in sync. Wrap app with `t-config-provider` so TDesign locale follows `locale`.

## Strings

- No hardcoded UI Chinese/English in views/components
- Add keys to `src/i18n/messages.ts` (`app.*` / `browse.*`) for both `zh` and `en`
- Call `t("dotted.key")` or `t("key", { n })` for `{n}` / `{name}` placeholders

```vue
<!-- ❌ -->
<span>获取官方示例</span>
<!-- ✅ -->
<span>{{ t("browse.fetchSamples") }}</span>
```

## Colors

Prefer **official TDesign tokens only** — do not maintain a parallel brand/shell palette.

- Page / panels / text / borders / hover / brand → `--td-bg-color-page`, `--td-bg-color-container`, `--td-text-color-*`, `--td-component-border`, `--td-brand-color*`, …
- Three.js clear color → read `--td-bg-color-page` (see `@/utils/viewportTheme`)
- Viewer overlay chrome may use the thin `--svg3dx-chrome-*` aliases in `global.css` (they map to `--td-*`)
- Never hardcode light-only hex (breaks dark mode)

```css
/* ❌ */
.item.active { background: #e4eefc; }
.panel { background: var(--studio-panel); }
/* ✅ */
.item.active { background: var(--td-brand-color-light); }
.panel { background: var(--td-bg-color-container); }
```
